 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch09_01_07\"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-id1512186\" data-alt=\"This illustration shows two receptor tyrosine kinase monomers embedded in the plasma membrane. Upon binding of a signaling molecule to the extracellular domain, the receptors dimerize. Tyrosine residues on the intracellular surface are then phosphorylated, triggering a cellular response.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20240910.161227/resources/c46c375615f40243e4a2ed562ee162251975abb5\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"This illustration shows two receptor tyrosine kinase monomers embedded in the plasma membrane. Upon binding of a signaling molecule to the extracellular domain, the receptors dimerize. Tyrosine residues on the intracellular surface are then phosphorylated, triggering a cellular response.\" width=\"280\" height=\"520\">\n</span>\n</figure>",
